  "solution": {
    "text": "If the order of skew-symmetric matrix is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, then the&nbsp;maximum number of distinct elements is <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>72</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math> (rejected)"
  }
